  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thepla"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is a Gujarati staple: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "thepla term ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "thepla-term"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The defining ingredient is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "methi ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "methi"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", fresh fenugreek. They are cooked on a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "tawa",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "tawa"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with a little oil. The dough must be soft enough to roll thin without tearing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If fresh fenugreek is unavailable, use 2 tbsp dried fenugreek leaves (kasuri methi). Soak in warm water for 10 minutes before adding to the dough."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
